SYNTHESIS
========================================================================
1. Fixed total n turns LRC into source reachability in a marked
   tournament on n vertices; after deleting the source observer, the
   target lives in tournament classes on m=n-1 vertices.
2. In an open source cell those m vertices lie in one arc of length
   1-2/n.  Relative to their arc order, backward edges form a Ferrers
   filter, and the fixed safe-arc length cuts Catalan many Ferrers
   signatures down to a much smaller interval-feasible menu.
3. Bounded speed clocks hit exactly the same open isomorphism classes
   for n=4..8.  Wall witnesses explain the extra closed-menu classes
   from S512/S520, so the true LRC object is an open tournament menu
   plus a compactified boundary fiber.
4. The problem at a particular n is therefore: prove every primitive
   arithmetic clock reaches this tiny Ferrers interval menu, or its
   compactified wall boundary, inside the A000568(n-1) class universe.
